  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between atomoxetine and Atrioventricular block NOS, mediated through synaptotagmin 17. Multiple paths indicate that atomoxetine affects synaptotagmin 17, which in turn contributes to the development of Atrioventricular block NOS. This mechanism is consistent across three different paths, with varying levels of confidence in the relationship, as reflected by the scores. Path_1734 provides the highest confidence, linking atomoxetine to synaptotagmin 17 and then to Atrioventricular block NOS, while Path_1735 and Path_1736 also support this pathway with lower scores. The evidence suggests that atomoxetine may influence the function of synaptotagmin 17, which could disrupt normal cardiac conduction and lead to Atrioventricular block NOS. However, the strength of the evidence is moderate, and further research is needed to confirm the direct causal relationship.",
